    "narrative": "Today's optimal lineup is anchored by **Jackson Merrill**, who boasts the day\u2019s highest projection at 75.10. His matchup against Trey Yesavage is our prime target, bolstered by a 13% boost from favorable platoon dynamics and a strong batting order placement. **Gunnar Henderson** (71.11) and **Kyle Tucker** (69.61) also stand as top-tier starts; while **Gunnar Henderson** faces a slight hurdle against an elite hold pitcher, the substantial park factor lift and his leadoff role keep him in the elite tier. Similarly, **Coby Mayo** (66.04) benefits from that same park advantage, turning his start into a high-upside play despite the looming presence of Noah Cameron.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the optimizer today was bypassing **Miguel Vargas**, who sits on the bench with a respectable 52.35 score. While his xwOBA of 0.398 is impressive, the combination of a tough matchup against Gage Jump and his assignment to the middle of the order left him just shy of the active roster threshold compared to the platoon-advantaged **Josh Jung** (58.72) and **Cole Carrigg** (59.76). We are also monitoring a 45% rain risk for **Jorge Polanco**, which adds volatility to his 52.62 score; should the weather shift, we are prepared to pivot to the bench. \n\nBeyond those pivots, we are tracking **Liam Hicks** (57.56) and **Drake Baldwin** (60.06), both of whom are projected for high efficiency despite the uncertainty of official lineups. **Andy Pages** (66.83) remains a high-confidence play against Brandon Pfaadt, specifically due to his ability to exploit the pitcher\u2019s slow delivery to potentially generate value in our scarcest category, stolen bases. We continue to hold **Josh Lowe**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, and **Brayan Rocchio** in reserve, keeping them ready should any late-scratch lineup announcements shift our strategy before the first pitch.",
